This folk poem of uncertain origin is often attributed to a woman named
Dora Johnson.

This version is transcribed from a tape recording of my great-grandfather
 reciting poetry.
I have kept some of his variations, namely the use of the expression
 "growing old" instead of "getting old", which appears to be the
 original wording.
There's something nice about the way "growing old" reads aloud, especially
 in an Appalachian accent.

